# d571 patch bundle — remove vestigial enforcement/deferrals handling

Protected file (`.claude/helpers/enforcement.cjs`) — Claude cannot write it; Codex applies.

## Evidence it is dead/vestigial

- The ONLY `deferrals` reference in `.claude/helpers/enforcement.cjs` is the reset-time
  cleanup block at lines 3540-3551 (verified: `grep -n deferral enforcement.cjs` returns
  only 3540-3547).
- `.hive-flow/enforcement/deferrals/` does NOT exist on disk (`ls` → ENOENT).
- NOTHING in the repo creates or writes that directory (repo-wide grep for
  `enforcement.*deferrals` across .cjs/.mjs/.js/.ts, node_modules excluded → no writers).
  Deferrals migrated to Knots (`scripts/deferral-ledger.cjs`); this block iterates a
  directory that is never populated.
- The block sits between the "Clear future band state files" loop and the "Clear per-agent
  state files" loop in the DEFAULT (unscoped) reset path. Removing it does not touch scoped
  resets (`resetStateScope`) or any other reset behavior — it only deleted files that never
  exist, so reset behavior is preserved exactly.

## Exact hunk to remove (unified diff, context anchored)

```diff
   for (const f of bandStateFiles) {
     try {
       const fp = path.join(ENFORCEMENT_DIR, f);
       if (fs.existsSync(fp)) fs.unlinkSync(fp);
     } catch {}
   }
-  // Clear deferral state directory
-  try {
-    const deferralsDir = path.join(ENFORCEMENT_DIR, 'deferrals');
-    if (fs.existsSync(deferralsDir)) {
-      const files = fs.readdirSync(deferralsDir);
-      for (const f of files) {
-        if (f.endsWith('.json')) {
-          try { fs.unlinkSync(path.join(deferralsDir, f)); } catch {}
-        }
-      }
-    }
-  } catch {}
   // Clear per-agent state files
   for (const baseDir of [ENFORCEMENT_DIR, LEGACY_ENFORCEMENT_DIR]) {
```

Net: remove 12 lines (the `// Clear deferral state directory` comment through its closing
`} catch {}`). No other lines change. No new references; `deferralsDir` is local to the block.

## Post-apply parity (Codex)

- `.claude/helpers/enforcement.cjs` is protected + engine-manifest-signed. After applying the
  hunk, regenerate/verify the engine manifest via `scripts/install-enforcement.mjs` so the
  signed engine surface matches the edited file (this is the recorded d571 unblock condition:
  "protected engine file: requires Codex patch + engine-manifest regen").
- Suggested verification after apply: re-grep `deferral` in enforcement.cjs → 0 hits; run any
  enforcement reset self-check to confirm reset still succeeds (the removed block only deleted
  a never-existent dir, so behavior is unchanged).
